      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nClarify the Known issue for Mistral 7B parallel tool calls in `docs/features/tool_calling.md`. The current text describes the problem but does not point readers to the existing workaround, which is already documented under a separate issue in the same section.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The Known issue for Mistral 7B parallel tool calls now explicitly references `examples/tool_chat_template_mistral_parallel.jinja`, which was previously only described under issue 2 of the same section.\n- No code changes; documentation-only.\n\n## Validation\n\nVerified with `mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3` on vLLM `v0.31.1rc1.dev114+gb49c921a2` (A100-80GB).\n\nFour test prompts, each requesting three tools (weather, forecast, air quality) with varying wording:\n\n| Template | Returns all 3 tool_calls |\n|----------|--------------------------|\n| `tool_chat_template_mistral.jinja` (default) | 2/4 prompts |\n| `tool_chat_template_mistral_parallel.jinja` | 4/4 prompts |\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Start the server with the default template:\n   ```bash\n   vllm serve mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3 \\\n     --tokenizer-mode mistral --load-format mistral --config-format mistral \\\n     --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser mistral \\\n     --chat-template examples/tool_chat_template_mistral.jinja \\\n     --port 8000\n   ```\n2. Send each of the four prompts with `tool_choice=\"auto\"` and count the returned `tool_calls`.\n3. Restart the server with `--chat-template examples/tool_chat_template_mistral_parallel.jinja` and repeat.\n\n## Details\n\nThe Known issue currently reads:\n\n> Mistral 7B struggles to generate parallel tool calls correctly.\n\nIt describes the symptom but not the workaround. The `tool_chat_template_mistral_parallel.jinja` template, which addresses exactly this problem, is documented under issue 2 (about the Transformers tokenization backend). Readers who only scan issue 1 may not realize a fix already exists.\n\nThis PR adds a one-line reference from issue 1 to the existing template description. The change is intentionally minimal: it does not restructure the section, only links the problem statement to the already-documented solution.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>",
